# Lane UI — backend SSOT

## Forbidden

- Client lane **placement/allocation engines** that duplicate backend `place_lane_assignments`, movement rules, or stamp logic
- Reintroducing inline **movement preview engines** — preview was removed; use backend score-sheet / schedule APIs
- Scattered lane label/slot formatting — centralize in shared helpers (`slotLabels`, `LaneAssignSelect`)

## Allowed

- Grid board presentation, drag-drop UX, PDF schedule display
- Pure layout/density helpers (`laneBoardGridModel`, `laneMovementGridDensity`)
- Backend endpoints: lane management, apply assignments, stamp, score-sheet projection

## UI shape

- Prefer **grid-only** lane panel over dual list+grid unless product explicitly needs both
- Persist **round scope** with assignment saves — don't drop round context between operations
- Team events: show team lane labels from API fields, not client recomputation from member rows

## Data fetching

- After check-in or lane assign mutations, invalidate the same downstream query sets as scoring (event complete, squad participants, lane tab data)
- Gate lane fetches on capability + tab visibility (`enabled` on queries)

## Tests

- Update Playwright lane specs when simplifying UI (grid-only, removed preview)
- Unit-test pure grid/model helpers only — not placement math on the client
